/E (The United Nations General Assembly \(UNGA\) has long stood as the most representative deliberative body of the international community, charged with safeguarding peace, security, and cooperation among Member States. When the Security Council is unable to act due to political deadlock, the UNGA may convene an Emergency Special Session \(ESS\) to address urgent threats to international peace and security. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
