/S /P
/E (The concept of humanitarian intervention has evolved significantly since the post-Cold War era. The failures in Rwanda 1994\) and Srebrenica 1995\) demonstrated the devastating consequences of international inaction in the face of mass atrocities. These tragedies catalyzed the development of the Responsibility to Protect doctrine, formally adopted at the 2005 World Summit.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The R2P framework established three pillars: first, the state's responsibility to protect its population; second, international assistance to help states fulfill this responsibility; and third, the international community's responsibility to take timely and decisive action when states manifestly fail to protect their populations from genocide, war crimes, ethnic cleansing, and crimes against humanity.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
