>>
endobj
224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This diversity in organization, objectives, and operational methods complicates both the negotiation of humanitarian access and the implementation of protection mandates. Humanitarian actors must navigate complex security environments in which armed groups may impose restrictions on movement, control aid delivery, or manipulate assistance for strategic purposes, all while civilian populations remain exposed to direct threats.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
226 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Moreover, the Syrian conflict highlights the operational and ethical problems faced by the international community in protecting civilians under conditions of fragmented authority. Negotiations with local armed actors require careful distinction between engaging for humanitarian purposes and providing political recognition, while ensuring that aid reaches populations without worsening local conflicts.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
