237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( At the same time, regional organizations such as the African Union and the Economic Community of Central African States \(ECCAS\) have played a critical role in facilitating negotiations between the government and armed factions, showing the importance of regional mediation in conflict resolution.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
238 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The 2019 Political Agreement for Peace and Reconciliation, concluded between the government and 14 armed groups with African Union support, demonstrated the potential of inclusive dialogue to reduce violence. However, despite this formal agreement, implementation has faced persistent challenges. Armed groups have frequently fragmented, with these fragmented factions rejecting the accords and continuing to engage in violent activities. This pattern highlights a recurring difficulty in peace processes involving non-state actors: while agreements may establish broad frameworks for peace, the lack of unified command structures among armed groups often worsens compliance.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
