255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The African Union \(AU\) has developed a range of innovative normative and operational frameworks to address the challenges posed by non-state armed groups, particularly in situations where state authority is weak and civilian populations face acute risks. One of the most significant instruments is the Kampala Convention on the Protection and Assistance of Internally Displaced Persons in Africa \(2009\), which is the first legally binding regional treaty of its kind. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Convention explicitly prohibits armed groups from engaging in practices such as forced displacement, attacks against humanitarian personnel, and the recruitment or use of children in armed conflict. It also obliges States Parties to adopt measures that ensure accountability for violations committed by both state and non-state actors, reinforcing international humanitarian law within a regional legal framework.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E <>
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
