/E (Armed non-state groups are bound by international humanitarian law IHL\) when they become parties to non-international armed conflicts. Common Article 3 of the Geneva Conventions and Additional Protocol II establish clear obligations for these groups, including prohibitions against violence against persons not taking an active part in hostilities.)
