/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The permanent members of the UNSC can block resolutions using the veto power. This power can result in a lack of unanimity, escalating the crisis at hand. In such situations, the UNGA can consider the matter. Although the UNGA cannot make legally binding resolutions, it can recommend collective measures to tackle a crisis.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
