<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The protection of civilians in conflicts involving non-state armed groups remains one of the most pressing dilemmas for the international community. Case studies highlight both the necessity and the difficulty of intervention, revealing the consequences of inaction, overreach, and inadequate post-conflict planning. Regional organizations and international frameworks have made important contributions, yet the gaps in legal clarity, operational mandates, and humanitarian access persist.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Emergency Special Session of the General Assembly offers a unique platform for Member States to overcome political gridlock and collectively address these gaps. Delegates are encouraged to approach the agenda with a balance of legal rigor, political sensitivity, and humanitarian urgency. The discussions and resolutions emerging from this committee can contribute not only to immediate protection needs but also to the long-term development of a more coherent and principled international response to armed conflicts.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
